$article=['date'=>'2027-01-08','slug'=>'adhd-or-poor-parenting','tag'=>'ADHD','category'=>'ADHD','breadcrumb'=>'ADHD or Poor Parenting?','meta_title'=>'ADHD or Poor Parenting? What Every Parent Should Know','description'=>'ADHD is not caused by poor parenting. Learn how clinicians separate persistent neurodevelopmental symptoms from stress, sleep and family context in children.','h1'=>'Is It ADHD or Just Poor Parenting? Separating the Two','dek'=>'Parenting does not cause ADHD, but families still deserve strategies that make daily demands easier to manage.','body'=><<<'HTML'
<p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-light">ADHD is a neurodevelopmental disorder, not the result of poor parenting. Diagnosis requires persistent symptoms beginning in childhood, appearing in multiple settings and impairing functioning. Genes play an important role, while research continues into other contributing factors.</p><h2>Why parents get blamed</h2><p>ADHD affects behaviours adults often treat as choices: waiting, stopping, remembering and completing routine tasks. Inconsistent performance can look deliberate because the child may focus intensely on something rewarding and struggle with an ordinary demand.</p><h2>What can look similar</h2><p>Sleep loss, anxiety, learning difficulty, stress and health conditions may produce inattention or dysregulation. An assessment considers these possibilities and gathers information beyond the home.</p><h2>Why context still matters</h2><p>Structure, clarity and support change how visible symptoms are. This does not mean the environment caused ADHD. It means adults can reduce unnecessary executive demands and teach skills more effectively.</p><h2>What assessment asks</h2><p>Clinicians examine development, duration, impairment and behaviour across home and school using interviews, reports and rating scales. No scan, parenting questionnaire or single attention task proves ADHD.</p><p>Explore <a href="/adhd/adhd-parent-support">ADHD parent support</a> without blame.</p>
HTML,'faqs'=>[['Can inconsistent discipline cause ADHD?','No. Parenting does not cause ADHD. Consistency may affect how manageable behaviour becomes, but diagnosis concerns a persistent neurodevelopmental pattern across settings.'],['Why can my child focus on games but not homework?','Attention in ADHD is influenced by reward, novelty, urgency and interest. Strong focus on a preferred activity does not rule out difficulty regulating attention elsewhere.'],['Can stress look like ADHD?','Yes. Stress, anxiety, poor sleep, learning difficulty and other conditions can resemble or worsen ADHD symptoms, which is why a thorough evaluation matters.'],['Does parent training mean parents caused the problem?','No. Parent support teaches ways to structure demands, reinforce skills and reduce conflict. It changes the environment around a real need rather than assigning blame.']],
